{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01W7aidt9wReQMEx7n37Epik","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed:\n\n**Task: `answers/09-architecture-provider-abstraction.md`** ✅\n\nWrote 10 interview-depth answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) for the Architecture & Provider Abstraction section. Highlights:\n\n- **Q1** — `IPaymentProvider` interface + `PaymentProviderRouter` factory with lazy adapter resolution; providers never leak into checkout UI\n- **Q2** — Concrete `StripeAdapter` and `AdyenAdapter` implementations showing how `mount`, `confirm`, `handleAction` normalise each PSP's radically different SDK API\n- **Q3** — `PaymentMethodConfig` server-driven data model expressing card/bank_transfer/wallet/BNPL without PSP field names; drives field rendering from config\n- **Q4** — Discriminated union `PaymentAction` handling inline Stripe 3DS vs full-page Adyen redirect, with sessionStorage state persistence across navigations\n- **Q5** — Thin-shim vs rich-unified-API tradeoff table; recommended \"lifecycle + capabilities\" middle path with opt-in capability flags for PSP-specific features\n- **Q6** — `FrontendPaymentError` with category enum + raw PSP payload; per-PSP normaliser maps (Stripe decline_code, Adyen refusal reason codes) preserving support-team detail\n- **Q7** — SDK registry with `dynamic import()`, preload triggered at route entry, Stripe async `<head>` script for fraud ML with chunk-name stability for CDN\n- **Q8 (Deep)** — Multi-PSP DOM: mount-all-at-init + CSS `display:none` toggling to preserve iframe state, EventTarget bus for normalised cross-SDK events, adapter cleanup contract\n- **Q9 (Deep)** — Failover architecture: server must pre-create both provider sessions; frontend timeout-race + `provider_unavailable` gate; detailed breakdown of where failover fundamentally breaks (card iframe isolation, idempotency risk, 3DS)\n- **Q10 (Deep)** — Braintree→Stripe migration: deterministic user hash routing, per-cohort chunk loading, cross-provider analytics tagging, migration-complete criteria with stratified success rate comparison\n\nNext up: `md-to-html` — run the Python script to generate all section HTML pages."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_read_input_tokens":51877,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":88,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5460d5-3632-4573-89d5-4609d7db0f17","uuid":"f521afe4-1738-43d9-a0d7-c558dab34301"}
